  # Objective
 To build a predictive model that can accurately identify the presence of Parkinson's disease based on biomedical voice measurements, which can assist healthcare professionals in the early diagnosis and treatment of the disease.

**Data Loading and Exploration**

# Parkinson’s Disease Data Set Information
The dataset for a Parkinson's project was obtained from the UC Irvine Machine Learning Repository (https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/174/parkinsons). 
This dataset is composed of a range of biomedical voice measurements from 31 people, 23 with Parkinson's disease (PD). Each column in the table is a 
particular voice measure, and each row corresponds to one of 195 voice recordings from these individuals ("name" column). It contains a total of 
24 columns (22 predictive features, name and status). The main aim of the data is to discriminate healthy people from those with PD, 
according to the "status" column, which is set to 0 for healthy and 1 for PD.  

